From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pokeplatinum-3ds <noreply@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 22:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Route 204's people once, Veilstone's maps as they load,
 Route 205's cliff (SDK_PORT_3DS)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Three things the wider field showed:

- Someone standing at the edge between two maps is in both maps' events,
  at the same place, so as to show from either: Route 204's two
  youngsters by the Ravaged Path and its sign are in the north's events
  and the south's. The people of the map beside were brought as well,
  so they showed twice, side by side as they turned and stepped about.
  Someone beside with the same picture at the same place as one of the
  player's map's own events isn't brought.

- Walking across a map's middle, the loaded maps move a column on, and
  the map now loaded at that side is read over several frames: nothing
  of it was drawn where the wider view reaches into it, a black square
  for a moment at the screen's edge as the player ran east in Veilstone
  City. Its strip by the other column, drawn while it was beside the
  loaded maps and still kept, is drawn till it's read (never read for
  this: after a warp all four maps are being read).

- Route 205's south end and Valley Windworks have their scenery maps
  south of them 5 and 9 tiles up, and the wider field's bottom lines saw
  past their cliffs there: a black band under the cliff. They're listed
  with Route 215 for the cliffs drawn on down, with a copy 2 tiles lower
  more for each 2 tiles the scenery is higher (Route 215's as before).

---
diff --git a/src/overlay005/fieldmap.c b/src/overlay005/fieldmap.c
index 9c96f2de..49053926 100644
--- a/src/overlay005/fieldmap.c
+++ b/src/overlay005/fieldmap.c
@@ -1163,6 +1163,29 @@ static void FieldMap_PortKeepHiddenInSight(FieldSystem *fieldSystem, enum MapHea
     }
 }
 
+// Whether someone of a map beside is in the player's map's own events too:
+// the same picture at the same place. Someone standing at the edge between
+// two maps is in both maps' events so as to show from either (Route 204's
+// two youngsters by the Ravaged Path, and its sign, in the north's events
+// and the south's: in each, its own one to talk to and the other's to be
+// seen). Brought from beside as well, they showed twice, side by side as
+// they turned and stepped about (2026-11-05).
+static BOOL FieldMap_PortInPlayersMap(FieldSystem *fieldSystem, const ObjectEvent *e)
+{
+    const ObjectEvent *own = MapHeaderData_GetObjectEvents(fieldSystem);
+    int i, n = (int)MapHeaderData_GetNumObjectEvents(fieldSystem);
+
+    for (i = 0; own != NULL && i < n; i++) {
+        if (ObjectEvent_GetGraphicsID(&own[i]) == ObjectEvent_GetGraphicsID(e)
+            && ObjectEvent_GetX(&own[i]) == ObjectEvent_GetX(e)
+            && ObjectEvent_GetZ(&own[i]) == ObjectEvent_GetZ(e)) {
+            return TRUE;
+        }
+    }
+
+    return FALSE;
+}
+
 // Room for the picture of someone beside: a berry patch's is the one its
 // berry shows now (its patch's in the save, by its event's data), with
 // room kept for what the player's map's own may still need.
@@ -1339,7 +1362,8 @@ static void FieldMap_PortNeighbours(FieldSystem *fieldSystem)
                 || (hiddenFlag != 0 && !(hiddenFlag >= MAP_LOCAL_FLAGS_START && hiddenFlag <= MAP_LOCAL_FLAGS_END)
                     && FieldSystem_CheckFlag(fieldSystem, hiddenFlag))
                 || !MapObject_PortInReach(ObjectEvent_GetX(e), ObjectEvent_GetZ(e), playerX, playerZ, 0)
-                || FieldMap_PortLeftHidden(beside[k], hiddenFlag)) { // (hidden as the player left their map)
+                || FieldMap_PortLeftHidden(beside[k], hiddenFlag) // (hidden as the player left their map)
+                || FieldMap_PortInPlayersMap(fieldSystem, e)) { // (the player's map's own copy of them)
                 continue;
             }
 
